    "notes": {
        "35d238be-fd0c-4710-a5c4-a6e168685d8a": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 448,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\n- The connected user must have an **email** in their Slack profile (users.info is read with the users:read.email scope).\n- The workspace must have **at least two active human members** (not bots, not Slackbot). Invite Users To Channel invites the first two of them with *Skip Invalid Users* on, so the connected user (already a member as the channel creator) is skipped and the other one is invited.\n- The invited member gets a Slack notification; the channel is archived at the end of the run."
        }
    }
